// --- bare FRECPE (ARM FPRecipEstimate), 87 rows ---------------------------------------
// The same qemu-aarch64 run as everything above, of the game's own `frecpe` instruction
// ALONE, without the two FRECPS refinements. The reciprocal rows above are the refined
// sequence, whose Newton steps can mask estimate differences (a wrong estimation constant,
// or a wrong subnormal partial normalization); these rows pin the estimate itself
// (Source::ReciprocalEstimate) bit-for-bit. 80 finite normals (both signs, both exponent
// ends, 64 by sweep), plus +/-0, +/-inf and two denormals. No NaN row: a generated NaN's
// sign would be the host's default NaN, not the ISA's.
//
